WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back
to "Late Night."

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.837 size:81% position:41%
With all of the talk
of financial stimulus,

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
many Americans
are still wondering

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.173 size:88% position:44% line:92%
when they'll receive aid

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.175
and where all their tax dollars
are going.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:12.379
Here with more on that is one of
our writers, Jeff Wright.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.447 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Horn honking ]

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Bell jingles ]
-Who's next?

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.818
-Hey, Government?
-What can I do for you, Citizen?

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I pay my taxes, right?
-You do.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's a lot, right?
-It could be more.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I've been out of work
for a while now,

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was wondering
what can I get

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:28.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
for being an active
American citizen?

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:30.096
-The best I can do for you is 6.
-$6,000?

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hell, no! $600!

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:33.733
-What?! $6,000 wasn't a no.
What you have been doing

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.435
with all the money I've been
giving you over the years?

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Mumbling ]

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.605 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What? Speak up!

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:39.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I brought some bombs.
Damn. okay?

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I bought some bombs
to impress some friends.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You called me?
-Oh, n-not right now, Bomb.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.811
Stay in the back.
I'll let you know what it's lit.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Alright.
-Look, Citizen.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.548 size:84% position:42%
Best I could do for you
is $600, maybe $2,000.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'mma need
at least 20% back.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why?
-'Cause I owe some people

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:52.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
some money!
Damn!

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oy.
-Next!

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:57.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, Government.
-Hey, Black Citizen.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'd like to trade my
"ancestors were a slave" card.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.996 size:75% position:38%
I was looking to get
40 acres and a mule.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
If not a mule,
I'll take a Toyota Camry.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Y'all still mad
about the slave thing?

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:07.467 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Plus, this car is old.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not even
in the best condition.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And whose fault is that?
-Best I could do

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
is maybe another
black president.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When?
-I've been dealing

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a headache
for the past four years,

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.777 size:78% position:39%
so you got to give me
at least two terms.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.313
-Yeah, alright, but he's got to
be full black this time.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:23.083
-How about his mom is black
and his dad is Canadian?

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Kind of like Drake.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Man, nobody want Drake
as president.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:28.455
-It's better than Kanye West.
-You right. Alright, fine.

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:30.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Next!
-Hey, Government.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.892
-Hey, Student.
Are you still switching majors?

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-You know, I might have a job

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.162
for you when you finish school.
-You lying.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You right.
What can I do for you?

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.133
-Can I speak to Student Loans?
-[ Whispering ] I'm not here.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He said he's not here
right now.

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.236 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I can see him.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, man,
I was just looking for you.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got my money?
-No, it's a pandemic.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm here to ask
for my money back.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whoa, don't say his name
in vain like that.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
You in here cussin'.
What money?

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The money I gave you
for school.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:55.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's virtual now,
so I don't see the point

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.851
of paying for a school
I technically don't even go to.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I already spent the money.
-On what?

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-An air fryer.
-An air fryer?

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.756
-Yeah, you, like, put food in it
and then it, like, heats it up.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-hey, I know
what an air fryer is!

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.293 line:92%
-So you know how cool it is!

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Look, man, why don't you
come back Tuesday?

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe I'll see
what I have for you.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.132 line:92%
-You said that last Tuesday.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.033
-You really gonna help him out?
-[ Scoffs ] No.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
-Are you done?

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:17.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause you still got to
sweep the back.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:19.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your break was over
five minutes ago.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't need this job.
-What?

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nothing.
-That's what I thought.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.410 line:92%
And make sure you lock the door.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause how did Black Citizen
get in here?

